# Shell scripts are sent to a Linux host — deploy.sh pipes a heredoc straight
# into a remote `bash -s`, where a CR at the end of every line is a syntax
# error. Checking them out with CRLF on Windows would break the deploy in a way
# that reads as a mysterious remote failure.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The recorder writes LF and the replayer strips whitespace, but keeping the
# rest of the tree consistent avoids diffs that are nothing but line endings.
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
